From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NotAlexNoyle <alexnoyle@icloud.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:28:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] configure warnings

Minor warnings.configure adjustment for the Jihad build.

Generated as a clean diff against UXP upstream  (Pale Moon); applies
independently (distinct files) to the pristine third_party/uxp submodule.

Imported from build/desktop/patches/0002-configure-warnings.patch.
---
 build/moz.configure/warnings.configure | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/build/moz.configure/warnings.configure b/build/moz.configure/warnings.configure
index 0704f94a09..8dd1b90ee0 100644
--- a/build/moz.configure/warnings.configure
+++ b/build/moz.configure/warnings.configure
@@ -88,6 +88,11 @@ check_and_add_gcc_warning('-Wno-error=deprecated-declarations')
 # false positives depending on optimization
 check_and_add_gcc_warning('-Wno-error=array-bounds')
 
+# GCC 9+ value-range analysis trips -Wformat-overflow on null %s args in debug
+# spew (e.g. js/src/jit/x64/BaseAssembler-x64.h:595); harmless for our build,
+# and js/src forces -Werror=format so this must be downgraded here to reach it.
+check_and_add_gcc_warning('-Wno-error=format-overflow')
+
 # can't get rid of those PGO warnings
 check_and_add_gcc_warning('-Wno-error=coverage-mismatch', when='MOZ_PGO')
 
